WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.740
 Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh.

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:05.740
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh.

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:11.572
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh.

00:00:11.572 --> 00:00:12.940
Isn't that so crazy?

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:17.440
Like, literally any other vowel
would just not have worked.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:20.530
We are about to talk about how
to access everything that's

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:22.625
inside of you to create a song.

00:00:22.625 --> 00:00:25.020
(SINGING): I just
want you close.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:28.820
 Music is more powerful than
any other medium, period.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:30.420
(SINGING): Where you
can stay forever.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.780
 If I wasn't an artist,
I would be a teacher.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:36.255
The coolest teacher of all time.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:42.367
We're going to go through
song writing, lyrics,

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:43.950
we're going to talk
about the process.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:47.790
So we are in my vocal booth.

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:50.250
My vocal warm ups
sound pretty crazy.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.110
Also going to bring
you into the studio,

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:55.630
talk production, how to
put everything together

00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:59.600
to really create that beautiful
piece that you want to create.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:02.560
If writing the song
is like the sketch,

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:05.140
arranging the song, and
particularly the vocals,

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:06.460
is like painting it.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:08.150
We're going straight
to the heart.

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:09.340
Boom, direct.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:11.230
To me, music is not technical.

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:14.118
It's emotional, and it
always has to emotional.

00:01:14.118 --> 00:01:17.541
We're talking about
freedom of expression.

00:01:17.541 --> 00:01:19.990
And sometimes you
have to get loud.

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:27.498
(SINGING): I keep on falling
in and out of love with you.

00:01:27.498 --> 00:01:29.290
 I'll never forget
the day they sang this.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:34.710
(SINGING): --loved someone
the way that I love you.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:36.090
 Every day, you're different.

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:37.980
Every day, you're growing.

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:39.700
Every day, you're better.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:42.960
I want to share with you
how to find your own voice,

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.270
how to trust it, too.

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:48.300
You know, you have something
to say the world wants to hear.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.084
The world needs it.

00:01:50.084 --> 00:01:53.050
Simple as that.

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:55.070
So if you're ready, I'm ready.

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:56.810
Are we ready?

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:57.310
Yes.

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:08.456
I'm Alicia Keys, and
this is my MasterClass.

00:02:08.456 --> 00:02:12.344
(SINGING): Promise you, baby.

00:02:12.344 --> 00:02:15.760
My love looks better on you.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:18.405
 Ting.

00:02:18.405 --> 00:02:20.570
I need that real bad.

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:23.710
Can we please put
the ting in there?

